    "key_points": [
      "Recursion is a method where a function calls itself to solve smaller instances of the same problem.",
      "Every recursive function must have at least one base case to stop the repeated calls.",
      "Each recursive call should move the problem toward the base case.",
      "The recursive case expresses the solution in terms of a smaller or simpler version of the problem."
    ],
    "difficulties": [
      "Students may find it difficult to understand how a function can call itself without stopping forever.",
      "Tracing recursive calls using a call stack can be challenging for beginners.",
