  "Personalized Recommendations": "Use visual supports such as graphic organizers, color-coded grammar charts, sentence diagrams, and storyboard-style planning pages. Connect lessons to her interests by using mystery novel excerpts, nature settings, and painting-based prompts, such as sketching a crime scene or describing a forest habitat. Provide a quiet study space with minimal distractions and include structured writing routines: plan, draft, edit, revise, and publish. Build on her vocabulary and reading comprehension strengths by having her analyze short passages and then write responses that apply grammar rules. Give frequent low-stakes writing opportunities, such as journaling, mystery clues, character sketches, or nature observations, and use specific feedback focused on grammar accuracy and clearer sentence structure."
}

