{
  "Learning Path Planning": "Phase 1 (Weeks 1-2) Modeling Foundations: Review ODEs, PDEs, dimensional analysis, and model assumptions; build small Python or MATLAB simulations with parameter sweeps and clear visualizations. Phase 2 (Weeks 3-6) Numerical PDEs: Implement finite difference, finite volume, and finite element methods for diffusion, advection, and wave equations; analyze stability, convergence, and error. Phase 3 (Weeks 7-10) Stochastic Modeling: Study Monte Carlo methods, stochastic differential equations, and uncertainty quantification; simulate a real-world stochastic process such as an epidemic, traffic, or financial risk model. Phase 4 (Weeks 11-14) Optimization and Control: Develop nonlinear optimization, parameter estimation, and optimal control models; apply them to resource allocation, engineering design, or operational planning. Phase 5 (Weeks 15-18) Data-Driven Modeling: Introduce surrogate models, reduced-order modeling, and physics-informed machine learning; combine numerical simulation with data fitting. Phase 6 (Weeks 19-24) Capstone Project: Design, implement, and present a complex applied model with real-world data; include code documentation, sensitivity analysis, peer review, and a portfolio-ready write-up. Ongoing activities: weekly hands-on problem solving, group code discussions, independent deep dives, and reflective modeling logs.",
