{
  "Learning Path Planning": "Phase 1 (Weeks 1-2): Build experimental safety and lab literacy through visual e-learning modules covering PPE, chemical handling, instrument identification, and lab notebooks. Phase 2 (Weeks 3-5): Complete guided hands-on spectroscopy experiments such as UV-Vis absorption, IR/Raman, and basic NMR, using step-by-step video checklists and virtual calibration simulations. Phase 3 (Weeks 6-9): Integrate her quantum-mechanics and computational strengths by running TD-DFT or vibrational-frequency calculations for the same molecules measured in lab, then compare simulated spectra with experimental data using visual overlays and uncertainty plots. Phase 4 (Weeks 10-14): Design a small independent project, for example a spectroscopic study of conformational changes or reaction kinetics, where she plans the experiment, performs data acquisition, troubleshoots instrument issues, and presents results with interactive data visualizations. Phase 5 (Weeks 15-16): Consolidate skills through a peer-reviewed experiment review, a lab-safety refresher, and a personal competency portfolio of checklists, raw data, reduced data, and reflections.",
